title: Speaking Tube
text: Shout into one pipe and listen. An old ship's voice pipe carries your words a long way, and what you hear back is not always quite what you said.
trick: the yellow target is at the top of a pipe that opens only onto the white beam's own lane: red and green are sent straight back by two head-on reflectors, recombine in the prism, run home along the white beam, and a splitter on that lane taps the returning yellow off up the pipe
motif: pictogram (a ship's voice pipes: a sealed pipe to the yellow target, a feed pipe up into a room, a hall below)
expect: reversals>=2, merges>=1
---
